  "rationale": "Existing fullstack/reviewer roles and Rust/security/contracts/UI guidance cover the selected stack. Active ADR6r5 acceptance, ADR7r1 escrow, ADR8r1 macOS confinement, ADR9r2 signed release/kernel image/UI64MiB+4096 budget, ADR10r1 conservative legacy adoption and ADR11r1 protected native recovery were independently reviewed. Updated security-boundaries covers macOS SDK ARC/blocks callback lifetime/deadlines, kernel peer/console/TTY checks, connection-bound ACK, durable deletion and bounded public escrow exchange. Actual ADR11 addition is solely alreadylocked cc1.11.1 host build edge (exact removal reproduces prior manifest/lock hashes) plus fixed SDK frameworks/libbsm; no host->office/pki or gateway->host edge, new crypto or browser secret surface. Whole build-script/native input pins and strict build-time release registry validation remain required; no arbitrary generated Rust include/helper exception. Existing tar0.4.46/flate21.1.11 and web rustix1.1.6 fs/std edges were scoped and verified without unrelated lock changes. AGENTS mandates root architecture/integration owner, maximum two disjoint source writers in separate worktrees and delegate-only caveman communication. Original authors and full acceptance retained. Current source-bound native/bootstrap and Chromium/debug fixtures are scoped evidence; authentic production publisher/platform/physical authentication/setup/service/Linux/WebKit, full current checks and fresh reviews remain mandatory. No production readiness claim. Fixed macOS libbsm SDK accessor link passed no-prompt compile/query; no Cargo version or reviewed presence mechanism changed.",
